# Example Tactical Data Link (XTDL) — a FICTIONAL binary format invented only to
# show the overlay shape. It is not a real standard and encodes nothing real.
# One 6-byte word, LSB-first bit ranges, decoded through the public `bits` wire.
format     xtdl-example
version    0.1.0
wire       bits
word_bytes 6
field  lat       0:0:21    linscale:1048575:90
field  lon       0:21:22   linscale:2097151:180
field  course    0:43:5    uint
